            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Tales by Dots and Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "6. Examine the statements below and justify if the statement is always true, sometimes true, or never true."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.13,
            0.845,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": "(i) Removing a value less than the median will decrease the median."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.172,
            0.827,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Including a value less than the mean will decrease the mean."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.196,
            0.717,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Including any 4 values will not affect the median."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.221,
            0.846,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Including 4 values less than the median will increase the median."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.268,
            0.845,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": "7. The mean of the numbers 8, 13, 10, 4, 5, 20, y, 10 is 10.375. Find the value of y."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.316,
            0.846,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.364,
            0.845,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": "9. Consider the data: 12, 47, 8, 73, 18, 35, 39, 8, 29, 25, p. Which of the following number(s) could be p if the median of this data is 29? (i) 10 (ii) 25 (iii) 40 (iv) 100 (v) 29 (vi) 47 (vii) 30"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.461,
            0.847,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": "10. The number of times students rode their cycles in a week is shown in the dot plot below. Four students rode their cycles twice in that week."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.531,
            0.711,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.685,
            0.823,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": "(i) Find the average number of times students rode their cycles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.708,
            0.82,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Find the median number of times students rode their cycles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.732,
            0.733,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Which of the following statements are valid? Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.757,
            0.656,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "(a) Everyone used their cycle at least once."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.781,
            0.718,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": "(b) Almost everyone used their cycle a few times."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.805,
            0.845,
            0.843
          ],
          "content": "(c) There are some students who cycled more than once on some days."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.847,
            0.845,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "(d) Exactly 5 students have used their cycles more than once on some days."
        },
